      "explain": "The six phases are grouped into two parts. The <strong>analysis phase (front end)</strong> breaks the source program apart and works out its meaning; the <strong>synthesis phase (back end)</strong> constructs the target program from that meaning. The front end depends on the <strong>source language</strong>, the back end depends on the <strong>target machine</strong>.",
