      "explain": "A <strong>macro</strong> is a named block of instructions defined once and then used many times by writing its name. The <strong>macro processor</strong> replaces every macro call with a full copy of the macro body — a process called <strong>macro expansion</strong> — <em>before</em> the assembler or compiler sees the program.",
